pst-9ij: expose the remaining three Multiconnect slot Customizer variables
(slotTolerance, dimpleScale, onRampEnabled) as multiconnectBack() module
parameters, so a use<>-ing model can set them per call instead of only via
file-scope globals `use <>` cannot import.

Follows 0002, which promoted backThickness / slotVerticalOffset /
connectVersion / quickRelease for the same reason. Those four plus these
three now cover every Customizer knob a mount needs; the standard set the
mounts expose is slot tolerance, retention (quickRelease), dimple scale and
on-ramp (pst-9ij pilots this on opengrid_bin; the LED holders + ego copy the
same @param block and pass-through call).

Named distinctly from the file-scope slotTolerance / dimpleScale /
onRampEnabled so neither shadows the other, and each defaults to its global,
so the file's own top-level Customizer call and any not-yet-updated caller
render exactly as before. No geometry changes at default arguments.

This file is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (QuackWorks, openGrid by David D); this patch is
a derivative under the same terms — see scripts/patches/README.md. Drop it if
upstream promotes these to module parameters.

